If $U$ is a symmetry, then $U\ket{E}$ has the same eigenvalue: $HU\ket{E}=EU\ket{E}.$ Since $E$ is a scalar, it commutes with $U$, and the original eigenvalue equation may be used: $\begin{aligned}
HU\ket{E}
&=EU\ket{E}\\
&=UE\ket{E}\\
&=UH\ket{E}.\end{aligned}$ Therefore $(HU-UH)\ket{E}=0.$

