If $L_i$ has no explicit time dependence, the Heisenberg equation gives $\frac{dL_i}{dt}
=i[H,L_i]=0
\qquad(\hbar=1).$ Thus symmetry generators are conserved charges. Spatial translation symmetry gives momentum conservation; rotation symmetry gives angular-momentum conservation.

