For bosonic modes labeled by $i,j$, $\begin{aligned}
&=0,&
[A_i^\dagger,A_j^\dagger]&=0,&
[A_i,A_j^\dagger]&=\delta_{ij}.\end{aligned}$ The labels may denote momentum, position, spin, or any complete one-particle basis. Because creation operators commute, $A_i^\dagger A_j^\dagger\ket{0}
=A_j^\dagger A_i^\dagger\ket{0}.$ The two-boson state is symmetric under interchange.

